{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779211824,"nonce":"rS9Nxh2e23WRA+9EdughYvXd5kQ=","message":"## Cross-Reference: task timelines and expression-valued parameters\n\nCreated `bd5aefb` — Spec: composable task timelines and expression-valued parameters.\n\nWhy this belongs in the Studio design map: the delayed-reach review exposed that Studio is still showing task internals as raw array/object fields (`epoch_len_ranges`, `target_on_epochs`, etc.) where the user needs an interaction surface. The broader requirement is a shared editor for values that may be constants, references, expressions, reusable functions, distributions, or schedules.\n\nKey UX direction recorded there:\n\n- delayed tasks should use an epoch/signal grid: epoch columns, signal rows, length controls, value/function cells, and preview;\n- reusable function shapes should live in a project/function library rather than be retyped in each field;\n- expression editing should be structured with autocomplete, units/shapes/types, previews, and dependency display, with raw text as an advanced path;\n- distributions need explicit sampling scope (`per trial`, `per replicate`, `per run`, `sweep`, etc.);\n- the same value editor should eventually power task signals, eval overrides, objective weights, component properties, acausal parameters, and sweep/replicate controls;\n- hidden properties that acquire runtime variation should be promotable to visible scenario controls or graph ports.\n\nRelevant precedents captured in the issue: Simulink Signal Editor, PsychoPy Builder routines/components, COMSOL user-defined functions, Onshape/Fusion parameter expressions, Houdini ramps, W\u0026B Sweeps, Modelica/Simscape, and KNIME expressions.\n\nThis should be treated as a cross-cutting Studio UX foundation that informs `0c46f69`, `85cec2c`, `b3ad156`, `a6efafc`, `6116155`, `e57ae1f`, and `c6c6da0`, not as a one-off replacement for the current delayed-reach fields.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}